{
	title: 'Show original session on forked messages',
	spec: 'Forked history retains the session ID where each copied record originated. Terminal and web headers of copied user messages, assistant text and thinking, and slash commands append (in <session-id>) at normal contrast. New messages in the current session have no marker. Forks of forks preserve the original ID rather than replacing it with the immediate parent. Both ordinary /fork and spawn mode fork use this behavior. Attribution survives reconnect and loading earlier history, remains distinct from sender identity, and does not alter message content or provider replay. Legacy histories without origin metadata remain readable; do not guess or backfill existing forks.',
